/// The full per-state animation table: one [`State`] per `S_*` index
/// from [`crate::engine::play::info`], in declaration order.
///
/// Every entry encodes one animation frame: which sprite to draw,
/// which frame letter (with the high bit `0x8000` flagging
/// full-bright), how long to stay on it, an optional action to run
/// when the actor enters the state, and which state to chain into
/// next. The thinker walks this graph one entry per tic.
///
/// # Cross-references
///
/// * `sprite` is an [`SPR_*`](SPR_TROO) index into [`sprnames`].
/// * `nextstate` is an `S_*` index back into this same table.
/// * `action` is one of the action functions imported above
///   (`A_Light0`, `A_Chase`, `A_Tracer`, ...), wrapped in its
///   [`StateAction`] variant by `action!`.
/// * `mobjinfo[].spawnstate`, `seestate`, `painstate`, `meleestate`,
///   `missilestate`, `deathstate`, `xdeathstate`, `raisestate` all
///   point into this table.
///
/// # Layout
///
/// `[State; NUMSTATES]` with [`NUMSTATES`] equal to the C
/// `statenum_t::NUMSTATES` sentinel; an entry with `tics == -1` and
/// `nextstate` equal to itself acts as a terminal/freeze state.
///
/// # Mutability
///
/// Mutability is required because `G_InitNew` rescales monster state
/// durations for `-fast` / nightmare (and Dehacked patches, `deh_state.c`,
/// overwrite individual entries in C). That is the only writer, and it runs
/// between levels; everything else reads entries by [`StateNum`] through
/// short `borrow`s. Map objects and psprites hold [`StateNum`]s, not
/// pointers, so the table needs no stable address.
///
/// # Per-entry comments
///
/// Each entry is followed by a `// S_FOO` trailer naming the
/// corresponding `S_*` constant, exactly matching the original C
/// source. Those are line comments rather than `///` doc comments
/// because array element expressions cannot carry rustdoc attributes.
